{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block pagecss %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/about.css">{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<section class="about-hero">
  <img class="about-hero-img" src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Hiker_in_the_top_of_mountain.JPG?width=1200" alt="Solo trekker in the mountains" width="1200" height="420" loading="eager">
  <span class="hero-credit" style="position:absolute;z-index:2;right:12px;bottom:8px;font-size:10px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.55);background:rgba(0,0,0,.35);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;">Photo: CC BY-SA 3.0 · Wikimedia Commons</span>
  <div class="about-hero-overlay"></div>
  <div class="about-hero-text">
    <div class="about-hero-eyebrow">Our story</div>
    <h1>Built for the trail.<br>Not the tour group.</h1>
    <p>Most trekking resources assume you have a guide, a group, and a travel agent. We don't.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="about-content">

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>The problem with existing guides</h2>
    <p>The best trekking resources on the internet are scattered across Reddit threads from 2019, agency blogs that exist to sell you a guided package, and travel forums where the most-upvoted answer is "just hire a guide."</p>
    <p>That's not useful if you want to go alone. Solo trekkers have different questions: Where is it genuinely safe to walk without a guide? Which teahouses are solo-friendly? What does the permit system actually cost if you do it yourself? What happens if your pace is faster than everyone else's?</p>
    <div class="pull-quote">
      <p>"The best trekking content online is written by people who want to sell you a tour. We write for people who want to skip the tour."</p>
    </div>
    <p>We research each trail as solo trekkers. We do the permit queue ourselves. We eat at the teahouses, check the bus timetables, and talk to the lodge owners. The result is a guide that answers the questions you actually have when you're planning alone.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Our content principles</h2>
    <ul class="principle-list">
      <li>
        <div class="principle-num">1</div>
        <div class="principle-body">
          <strong>Solo-first, not solo-adapted</strong>
          <span>Every section is written with a solo trekker's perspective as the default. Groups are the edge case.</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="principle-num">2</div>
        <div class="principle-body">
          <strong>Real costs, not ranges</strong>
          <span>We publish actual costs for permits, teahouses, food, and transport from our own trips. Updated annually.</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="principle-num">3</div>
        <div class="principle-body">
          <strong>No affiliate links in the trail guide</strong>
          <span>Our trail content is not written to convert you into a gear sale. We link to official sources only.</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="principle-num">4</div>
        <div class="principle-body">
          <strong>Transparent content roadmap</strong>
          <span>We publish which trails are next. No surprise launches, no vague "coming soon."</span>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="principle-num">5</div>
        <div class="principle-body">
          <strong>Offline-ready for Pro members</strong>
          <span>Every full guide includes a downloadable PDF and GPX file. Because mountain wifi is not a planning assumption.</span>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Where we're going</h2>
    <p>The Solo Trail covers {{ liveStats.liveCount }} trails live today across {{ liveStats.liveRegions }} regions in {{ liveStats.liveCountries }} countries — anchored by our full Annapurna Base Camp guide and a completely-mapped Maharashtra, India (forts, jungle trails, peaks, waterfalls, and coastal sites). Here's what's next.</p>

    <div class="roadmap-stats">
      <div class="rm-stat"><div class="rm-stat-num">{{ liveStats.liveCount }}</div><div class="rm-stat-label">Live guides</div></div>
      <div class="rm-stat"><div class="rm-stat-num">{{ liveStats.liveCountries }}</div><div class="rm-stat-label">Countries</div></div>
      <div class="rm-stat"><div class="rm-stat-num">{{ stateStubs.length }}</div><div class="rm-stat-label">States queued next</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="roadmap">
      <div class="roadmap-group-title">In production</div>
      {% for t in trailsList %}{% if t.status == "coming-soon" %}
      <div class="roadmap-row">
        <div><div class="roadmap-trail">{{ t.name }}</div><div class="roadmap-region">{{ t.country | countryFlag }} {{ t.region }} · {{ t.maxAltitudeM | commaNum }}m</div></div>
        <span class="roadmap-tag tag-next">Next up</span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      <div class="roadmap-group-title">Planned</div>
      {% for t in trailsList %}{% if t.status == "planned" %}
      <div class="roadmap-row">
        <div><div class="roadmap-trail">{{ t.name }}</div><div class="roadmap-region">{{ t.country | countryFlag }} {{ t.region }} · {{ t.maxAltitudeM | commaNum }}m</div></div>
        <span class="roadmap-tag tag-planned">Planned</span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% for s in stateStubs %}
      <div class="roadmap-row">
        <div><div class="roadmap-trail">{{ s.name }}</div><div class="roadmap-region">🇮🇳 India — next state on our list</div></div>
        <span class="roadmap-tag tag-planned">Planned</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>Questions about a trail, corrections to a guide, or just want to say you completed ABC alone — reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@thesolotrail.com" style="color:var(--forest);font-weight:500;">hello@thesolotrail.com</a>.</p>
    <p>If you're an experienced solo trekker and want to contribute a guide review or local knowledge, we want to hear from you.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="about-cta">
    <h2>Start planning your solo trek</h2>
    <p>Browse our current trail guides or go Pro for offline access and new guides the moment they drop.</p>
    <div class="btn-cta-row">
      <a href="/trails/" class="btn-ghost">Browse trails</a>
      <a href="/downloads/" class="btn-solid">Get Trail Kits →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

{% endblock %}
